## Why the shipped fix did not move the trajectory (measured, this run)
RCA hypothesis 'gradeable required_concepts + runner dimensions => unlock' is STRUCTURALLY
satisfied but empirically INSUFFICIENT:
- All 38 distinct required_concepts WERE served as practice items during days 1-60.
- Every (target-goal concept, edge dimension) pair has served evidence: all 170 hard
  goal->goal edges pass the concept-coverage test computed from the walk's served
  (cid, #modality) pairs.
- Yet prereq_satisfied NEVER fired: engine (apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:2155-2210)
  requires min over ALL of the target goal's required_concepts to reach required_state
  (supported/independent) on the edge dimension, evaluated on derive_mastery_in_pack rows.
  Unlock is therefore gated by derived MASTERY STATE thresholds/decay, not by evidence
  existence. The 60-day walk unlocked exactly the same 20 units the broken pack unlocked.
=> Next diagnosis (not this card): instrument goal_derived_state at day 30/60 - dump the
   derived state of the 38 shared concepts (min per goal); the suspect is that the MIN of 4
   shared words never reaches the required_state within 60 days (paced spaced-repetition
   promotion), or unit_goal_locked reads a path distinct from prereq_satisfied's.
   A pack-data remedy may be legitimate (fewer/thinner required_concepts per goal, or
   required_state 'supported' instead of 'independent' on ladder edges) - it is pack content,
   in-scope, and cheap to iterate: goals.yaml is one file, re-walk is ~8 min.
